{
  "caseId": "field-signal-v1",
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "C_TARGET",
      "path": "protocol/target.md",
      "text": "ID C_TARGET. Controlling protocol TARGET for this fictional device trial.\n[C_Q] Question: what percentage of attempted signal detections succeed in the defined launch cohort and commissioning-relative interval?\n[C_POP] Include every unit whose first accepted commissioning event is at or before global time0. First telemetry availability is not commissioning eligibility. A device can belong even if it first reports later.\n[C_ANCHOR] Anchor each included unit at its first accepted commissioning event. Rejected commissioning attempts and later calibration do not move the origin.\n[C_WINDOW] Count attempts at offsets0 through2 days relative to that anchor, inclusive at both ends.\n[C_METRIC] Pool all included attempts; success percentage is100 times the number of pass outcomes divided by all included attempts. A pass is a successful signal detection. A fail is an unsuccessful detection. An empty denominator yields null, never0.\nPopulation, anchor, window and metric meanings are independent roles. Exact baseline percentage equality does not establish semantic equivalence.\n",
      "sha256": "0ede33f75832e48126a8d3dd7c03e7398ef20363228e81b22a8404c6bfd50607"
    },
    {
      "id": "L_BIND",
      "path": "implementations/L/bindings.md",
      "text": "ID L_BIND. Selected implementation L, immutable baseline binding.\n[L_EXEC] Population uses C_POP, anchor uses C_ANCHOR, window uses C_WINDOW and metric uses C_METRIC from protocol/target.md. L directly implements TARGET. A later archive copy with the same display name is not bound by L.\nL's selected definition identities remain explicit when trial data change.\n",
      "sha256": "0d52c3462c25e085b6ac309fe69f1e9e876d0a153aeeda8ec1e52249e7445ac4"
    },
    {
      "id": "U_POP_DOC",
      "path": "implementations/U/population.md",
      "text": "ID U_POP_DOC. Selected definition owned by U.\n[U_POP] Include units whose firstTelemetryTime is at or before global time0. Late telemetry units are outside this implementation cohort.\n",
      "sha256": "a00083d7c76d73d04eebc45e7ef45af662bae8eb1ed1598db665bd06e1d0b6c1"
    },
    {
      "id": "U_TIME_DOC",
      "path": "implementations/U/timing.md",
      "text": "ID U_TIME_DOC. Selected definition owned by U.\n[U_ANCHOR] Anchor each included unit at its first accepted calibration event, not its commissioning event.\n[U_WINDOW] Use offsets0 through2 days inclusive, exactly as C_WINDOW defines the numeric bounds.\n",
      "sha256": "fb5119f1bb1f225862c350ee9f614148101f529e4755aaeebd1b7d614d494026"
    },
    {
      "id": "U_METRIC_DOC",
      "path": "implementations/U/metric.md",
      "text": "ID U_METRIC_DOC. Selected definition owned by U.\n[U_METRIC] Report100 times fail outcomes divided by all included attempts, pooling attempts. Display the result as success percentage.\n",
      "sha256": "260122a30b53a46e4f794c688d6b5bf3abd518b47bbf87da8488ab25c158afaa"
    },
    {
      "id": "U_BIND",
      "path": "implementations/U/bindings.md",
      "text": "ID U_BIND. Selected implementation U, immutable baseline binding.\n[U_EXEC] Population uses U_POP from implementations/U/population.md. Anchor uses U_ANCHOR and window U_WINDOW from implementations/U/timing.md. Metric uses U_METRIC from implementations/U/metric.md.\n[U_ALIAS] The display term ready means telemetry available for U_POP but commissioned for C_POP. These are different predicates, not aliases. This selected execution does not use archive/success-definition.md.\n",
      "sha256": "c9e2f4c03af83b548a997f048f87fd70c9a05f3fa5ca78a26e432f4f99ded82d"
    },
    {
      "id": "ARCHIVE_OLD",
      "path": "archive/success-definition.md",
      "text": "ID ARCHIVE_OLD. Archived definition, not selected by L, U or TARGET.\n[OLD_SUCCESS] The historical display name success percentage once meant failures as a fraction of attempts. This file is not a runtime binding. Similar names are not artifact identity. Repairing this archive cannot repair the selected U metric.\n",
      "sha256": "ca6b634143e9a0c8f7adf5879a01a4725d52a91ca1c1eba68d0c47afe6a18948"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTROL",
      "path": "controls/authorization.md",
      "text": "ID CONTROL. Probe and repair authority.\n[P_SCOPE] Only the five supplied trial seeds may be used. Their typed snapshots are complete; omitted measurements are absent rather than unobserved. Each permitted seed changes only its declared unit events, telemetry or raw outcome facts. Definitions and artifact bindings remain fixed during investigation.\n[P_REQUIRED] Consume all five seeds, including the rejected-retry control and the interacting coincidence control. A headline equality in the interaction trial does not reject independently supported mechanisms.\n[P_COST] Every seed costs1; when equally discriminating choose ascending seed ID. This is probe order, not event order.\n[R_SCOPE] Only U's three selected definition files population.md, timing.md and metric.md may be repaired. Keep clause identities U_POP/U_ANCHOR/U_METRIC and the existing execution bindings. Do not edit TARGET, L, archive, window bounds or raw trial data.\n[R_MIN] Minimize distinct selected definition sites edited after all source-backed semantic causes are covered. All three roles must agree with TARGET for baseline and every supplied trial; matching numbers alone is insufficient.\n[OUTPUT] Contrast IDs CP_POP, CP_ANCHOR, CP_WINDOW, CP_METRIC correspond to those roles. Hypothesis IDs HP_POP, HP_ANCHOR, HP_METRIC correspond to the three differing roles. Root cause definition IDs are U_POP, U_ANCHOR, U_METRIC. Repair proposal ID REPAIR_U; edit IDs FIX_POP, FIX_ANCHOR, FIX_METRIC. Generated local-decision IDs are arbitrary unique strings and require real trace consumption.\n",
      "sha256": "8195033db026899f925e065791285c885803b8876b6343f524b7e50f3e518231"
    },
    {
